WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.718
Expert performance is built through practice that resembles the demands of real work while still creating room for improvement.

2
00:00:08.718 --> 00:00:15.601
Deliberate practice starts with a specific capability, a clear standard, focused effort, feedback, and correction.

3
00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:20.189
It is not just doing the job again and again.

4
00:00:20.189 --> 00:00:25.236
It is designing repetition so weak points become visible and fixable.

5
00:00:25.236 --> 00:00:32.119
Scenario training, simulations, rehearsal, drills, worked examples, and edge-case practice all serve different purposes.

6
00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.248
A worked example shows how a strong performer thinks.

7
00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:38.543
A drill strengthens one component.

8
00:00:38.543 --> 00:00:41.755
A simulation combines components under realistic constraints.

9
00:00:41.755 --> 00:00:49.555
Edge-case practice teaches the performer what changes when the usual pattern is incomplete, misleading, or missing.

10
00:00:49.555 --> 00:00:51.849
Repetition with variation is important.

11
00:00:51.849 --> 00:00:55.979
Exact repetition can build fluency, but variation supports transfer.

12
00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:01.944
Change the time pressure, available information, stakeholder, tool failure, handoff point, or exception.

13
00:01:01.944 --> 00:01:07.450
The learner must recognize the underlying principle instead of memorizing one scenario.

14
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.956
This helps reduce brittle performance that only works in a familiar example.

15
00:01:12.956 --> 00:01:16.626
Practice should be separated from production when possible.

16
00:01:16.626 --> 00:01:18.462
Production work rewards finishing.

17
00:01:18.462 --> 00:01:19.838
Practice rewards improving.

18
00:01:19.838 --> 00:01:29.015
A good practice system gives people permission to slow down, repeat, compare, and receive feedback before returning to live work.

19
00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:36.815
The final test is transfer: does the practice make real performance more reliable, adaptable, and evidence-informed?
